::ingredients

(butter; unsalted) 5tsp
(flour) 5tsp
(milk, whole) 1l
(salt) to taste
(pepper) to taste
(nutmeg) 1 pinch

::equipment

(pot)

::instructions

(butter) <put, in (pot)>
    <melt, slowly, medium-low heat>
{roux} = (butter) + (flour)
    <stir, medium-low heat> ?= lightly golden brown and nutty smelling
Repeat [
    {roux}
        + (milk) about a glass
        <stir, constantly> ?= combined
]
until thick sauce forms and new milk combines easily
Never stop stirring during the gradual milk additions; skipping this stage leaves lumps of roux that are hard to remove.
{sauce}
    + (milk) rest of
<reduce heat, to low>
{sauce} <stir, including the pot corners to prevent burning> ?= desired thickness
    <taste>
    + (salt) + (pepper)
    <season, to liking>
    + (nutmeg, preferably freshly grated)

::story

